;; EXPECT: check-failed
;; LAZY_AC_EQS: on
;; Book chapter 16: lazy completion does NOT help anti-unification.
;;
;; The same program a third time, run with `--lazy-ac-eqs`. The result is identical
;; to the plain run, size 5 with the same `Variants` node, and the size-2 assertion
;; fails exactly as it does there. The test suite asserts that failure, because it is
;; the point of the file.
;;
;; The reason is the trigger. Lazy completion opens its transaction when an equality
;; check asks a question plain congruence cannot answer, and `(check (= a b))` and
;; `(check (!= a b))` are the only two commands that count. `antiunify` and `checkau`
;; are not equality checks. They close any open transaction, which restores the
;; graph and discards whatever completion had derived, and only then does the solver
;; take its snapshot. So the snapshot it searches is the plain graph.
;;
;; That is not an oversight to route around by making the solver open the transaction
;; itself. Look at what it would cost. The solver has one node per reachable ordered
;; class pair, and there is no single pair to install as the completion goal, because
;; the whole point of the search is that it does not know in advance which pairs
;; matter. Making it lazy would mean one goal-directed completion search per visited
;; pair, each inside its own mark-and-restore, and the accumulated state that makes
;; consecutive equality checks cheap would be thrown away between pairs. Eager
;; completion pays the closure once for the whole graph and hands the solver a
;; snapshot it can read with `find`.
;;
;; So the three modes are not three points on one speed axis. Plain and lazy give
;; the solver the same, incomplete, relation. Eager is the one that changes what the
;; answer means.

(sort E)
(function add (E) E :assoc :comm)
(function g (E) E)
(function a () E)
(function b () E)
(function c () E)
(function d () E)
(function n () E)

(union (add a b) c)
(union (add a b d) n)

(let l (g n))
(let r (g (add c d)))

(antiunify l r :algorithm exact)

;; Not reached: the snapshot is the plain graph.
(checkau l r :max_size 2 :algorithm exact)
